{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792416272,"nonce":"tobsRY5zv+L5SDj7SJezizPggI8=","message":"CanvasKit investigation for the Git history graph\n\nUser asked to combine ashui-canvaskit interactive drawing with Ashui components for a Git tree graph. UI ownership is RayScript; the editor keeps the generic Ashui rendering bridge. This also resolves the earlier SCM-renderer question in favor of the existing extension architecture.\n\nVerified against RayDE's current Ashui pin ddb5ee441c912ab7f7bd336276a385df7bb000f1. scripts/deps.sh already includes canvaskit/haxe. The pinned CanvasKit.hx and Viewport2D.hx match the sibling's current implementations; no dependency update is needed for the inspected 2D features.\n\nAvailable APIs:\n- CanvasKit draw(ctx, kit): GPU-backed paths/shapes/text in content coordinates, under Ashui layout/clipping/opacity. DrawContext.strokePath plus Path.cubicTo handles branch/merge edges; circles and text cover commits and labels.\n- Viewport2D: coordinate conversion, pointer-centered zoom, panning, fit/reset and eased moves. CanvasKit handles wheel/trackpad input, middle/right pan, selection and hover.\n- region(id, bounds), Selection2D and SpatialIndex supply hit testing, click/hover callbacks, modifier selection and marquee selection. visible(bounds) supports culling. Repaint follows signal changes; continuous animation is optional.\n- Sibling tools/demo/Canvas2D.hx already composes CanvasKit with Button, Select and ToggleSwitch overlays. Git topology should stay fixed; dragging commits should not edit the DAG.\n\nCurrent gaps are in RayDE, not the drawing library. Preview.make creates plain nodes and maps unknown tags to div. Tags does not expose canvas-kit, and Preview.hook currently forwards only click, pointerDown/Up and pointerEnter/Leave. The component catalog is not generally bridged yet. The Git native module also lacks revision-walk/commit/ref APIs; its current operations are repository/status/diff.\n\nProposed reusable bridge:\n- Expose a generic canvas-kit element accepting a retained, serializable drawing scene: batched path/circle/rect/text operations, hit regions and full-scene bounds. Do not create a Git-specific renderer.\n- RayScript owns commit records, deterministic DAG lane placement, filters, selection and actions. It updates the scene when data/layout changes.\n- The Haxe CanvasKit adapter caches decoded drawing data and owns local viewport gestures, painting, hit testing and hover/selection visuals. Exchange semantic events (region ids, selected ids, viewport changes when needed), not synchronous per-frame calls across the process boundary.\n- Expose ordinary Ashui components through the same generic bridge for filters, menus, search, commit details and list interaction. A shared selected commit id links the graph and details.\n- Keep full scene bounds separate from culled hit regions. CanvasKit.fitContent uses the current registered index, so a culled graph should fit through Viewport2D.fit with its full bounds.\n- Add paged libgit2 revwalk/commit-parent/ref bindings, then deterministic lane assignment and incremental history pages. Keep native reads on the existing library lane, outside painting.\n\nProof: created an isolated Haxe-side probe, not an installed Git extension or a finished RayScript bridge. Source retained at RayDE/bin/GitGraphProbe.hx; program bin/git-graph-probe.hl. It uses fixture commits with forks/merges, CanvasKit curves/nodes/labels, Ashui Select and Buttons, and a reactive Ashui details panel. Offscreen checks pass in dark and light themes for hover, commit selection, button and wheel zoom, actual middle-button panning, and fit zoom/position. Probe panning disables momentum for deterministic fit assertions. Both snapshots were visually inspected; row controls are 32 px high.\n\nPreviews:\n- bin/snapshots/rayde-dark-git-canvaskit-probe.png\n- bin/snapshots/rayde-light-git-canvaskit-probe.png\n\nCompile uses the existing scripts/deps.sh ui_args, -cp bin, -main GitGraphProbe, -hl bin/git-graph-probe.hl. Run with ASHUI_SNAPSHOT_DIR set to bin/snapshots and ash --preset application bin/git-graph-probe.hl. No windows opened, no sibling source edited, no native/Cargo build or new worktree. RayDE tracked source remains clean. This records the verified approach for the Git UI work; it does not claim the runtime bridge or real repository history graph is implemented.","files":null}]}